    "short": "Gurdwara Karamsar (Punjabi: ਗੁਰਦੁਆਰਾ ਕਰਮਸਰ) is a prominent Sikh gurdwara complex in Rara Sahib, Ludhiana district, Punjab, India, attributed to Sant Isher Singh Ji and Sant Kishen ",
    "description": "Gurdwara Karamsar (Punjabi: ਗੁਰਦੁਆਰਾ ਕਰਮਸਰ) is a prominent Sikh gurdwara complex in Rara Sahib, Ludhiana district, Punjab, India, attributed to Sant Isher Singh Ji and Sant Kishen Singh Ji, two Brahmgiani Sikh saints of the 20th century. Gurdwara Karamsar was established in 1936 and was named after Sant Karam Singh Ji, a revered saint of Hoti Mardan and the predecessor of Sant Attar Singh Ji of Reru Sahib, who was the teacher of Sant Isher Singh Ji and Sant Kishen Singh Ji.",
